  "title": "The €700,000 wealth tax line",
  "source_article": "late-tax-penalties.txt",
  "source_slug": "wealth_tax_en",
  "post_text": "Spain runs a second property-owner tax most people never meet. If your Spanish assets are drifting toward 700,000 euros, you should know exactly where the line sits.\n\nWealth tax applies to residents and non-residents alike, measured on total assets. Below 700,000 euros, nothing is owed. Above it, the tax bites incrementally, only on the value over the line, at progressive rates from 0.2 to 2.5 percent. No sale, no income, no trigger. Owning is enough.\n\nNow the twist: where you own matters as much as what you own. The tax is shaped by local government, and Madrid applies a 100 percent discount. Identical assets, zero bill. Residents who live in their Spanish home also get an extra 300,000 euro allowance on that main home.\n\nWho actually gets caught? Two profiles. Non-residents holding one high-value property. And owners whose several Spanish assets, the apartment, the garage, the plot, quietly add up past the threshold without anyone doing the sum.\n\nThat last part is the real danger. Nobody sends a warning when you cross the line. The threshold does not announce itself.\n\nThe discipline costs one hour a year: total your Spanish assets. Anywhere near the line, get advice for your specific region, because in this tax, geography changes everything.\n\nGeneral information, not tax advice.\n\n#SpanishTax #WealthTax #SpainProperty",
