  "title": "Your NRA number needs renewing yearly",
  "source_article": "nra-deadline.txt, rental-rule-changes.txt",
  "post_text": "Renting out in Spain? Your NRA registration number is not a one-time formality. For 2025 rentals, the renewal window is 1 February to 2 March 2026.\n\nThe NRA, Numero de Registro de Alquiler, came into force on 1 July 2025. Every short, mid-term and tourist rental needs one, displayed on the listing, or you cannot legally advertise on the big platforms.\n\nWhat surprises owners is the annual filing. Even if you rented the place out once all year, you must renew, and the renewal is a report:\n\nConfirmation the property is still used for rentals.\nAny ownership changes.\nThe year's rental activity: the different lets and their lengths.\nThe reasons for each stay: holiday, work, studying.\nConfirmation that safety and habitability standards are maintained.\n\nYou file through the Land Registry your property is registered under. If you already hold an NRA, expect a reminder email in January.\n\nTwo practical warnings. The registry websites can be temperamental: in Valencia, the forms famously only download on a Microsoft computer, so some owners end up going in person. And your community can close the door entirely: if the building has voted to ban tourist rentals, no registration code will be issued.\n\nThe habit that makes all of this painless: keep a running log of every rental, dates, length and reason for stay, as the year goes. February you will thank August you.\n\nGeneral information, not legal advice.\n\n#HolidayRental #SpainProperty #SpanishHomeOwners",
